        "slug": "q-a",
        "updatedAt": "2022-01-02T14:24:09Z"
    },
    "closed": true,
    "closedAt": "2025-07-23T12:27:02Z",
    "comment_count": 2,
    "comment_data": [
        {
            "author": {
                "avatarUrl": "https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/24854248?u=d09fd974c6720eba3039db6beb2f1c1efecdb51d&v=4",
                "login": "echasnovski",
                "resourcePath": "/echasnovski",
                "url": "https://github.com/echasnovski"
            },
            "authorAssociation": "MEMBER",
            "body": "It should be possible in theory. It would require:\r\n- Create new scratch buffer.\r\n- Set its source to [`gen_source.none()`](https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/blob/432a0614f8dc38715892b0eec537716457ea4c2f/doc/mini-diff.txt#L557). Like `vim.b.minidiff_config = { source = MiniDiff.gen_source.none() }`.\r\n- Set buffer text to the text from `HEAD`.\r\n- Set reference text to the text from `0123abc` commit (via [`set_ref_text()`](https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/blob/432a0614f8dc38715892b0eec537716457ea4c2f/doc/mini-diff.txt#L507)).\r\n\r\nIf this is something to be used in a more interactive manner (like custom action for applying hunks), creating a [full custom source](possible in theory by creating [custom source](https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/blob/432a0614f8dc38715892b0eec537716457ea4c2f/doc/mini-diff.txt#L335) might be a better solution.\r\n\r\nI remember seeing an example of something similar somewhere in issues/discussions, but can not find it. And I am afraid, there are no plans to have something like this built-in.",
            "bodyHTML": "<p dir=\"auto\">It should be possible in theory. It would require:</p>\n<ul dir=\"auto\">\n<li>Create new scratch buffer.</li>\n<li>Set its source to <a href=\"https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/blob/432a0614f8dc38715892b0eec537716457ea4c2f/doc/mini-diff.txt#L557\"><code class=\"notranslate\">gen_source.none()</code></a>. Like <code class=\"notranslate\">vim.b.minidiff_config = { source = MiniDiff.gen_source.none() }</code>.</li>\n<li>Set buffer text to the text from <code class=\"notranslate\">HEAD</code>.</li>\n<li>Set reference text to the text from <code class=\"notranslate\">0123abc</code> commit (via <a href=\"https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/blob/432a0614f8dc38715892b0eec537716457ea4c2f/doc/mini-diff.txt#L507\"><code class=\"notranslate\">set_ref_text()</code></a>).</li>\n</ul>\n<p dir=\"auto\">If this is something to be used in a more interactive manner (like custom action for applying hunks), creating a [full custom source](possible in theory by creating <a href=\"https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/blob/432a0614f8dc38715892b0eec537716457ea4c2f/doc/mini-diff.txt#L335\">custom source</a> might be a better solution.</p>\n<p dir=\"auto\">I remember seeing an example of something similar somewhere in issues/discussions, but can not find it. And I am afraid, there are no plans to have something like this built-in.</p>",
            "bodyText": "It should be possible in theory. It would require:\n\nCreate new scratch buffer.\nSet its source to gen_source.none(). Like vim.b.minidiff_config = { source = MiniDiff.gen_source.none() }.\nSet buffer text to the text from HEAD.\nSet reference text to the text from 0123abc commit (via set_ref_text()).\n\nIf this is something to be used in a more interactive manner (like custom action for applying hunks), creating a [full custom source](possible in theory by creating custom source might be a better solution.\nI remember seeing an example of something similar somewhere in issues/discussions, but can not find it. And I am afraid, there are no plans to have something like this built-in.",
